>
  <p class="blog-lede" slot="lede">
    This guide supports shoppers on the <strong><a href="/">Kakobuy Spreadsheet</a></strong> directory at kakobuy-cn.com. If you've noticed your shipping quotes to Germany, France, or the Netherlands creeping up this year, it's not just fuel prices. As of <strong>January 1, 2026</strong>, the EU's <strong>Emissions Trading System (ETS)</strong> has expanded to cover 100% of shipping emissions. This legislative shift has introduced a mandatory "Green Surcharge" on every parcel entering the bloc.
  </p>

  <h2>100% Coverage: The 2026 Milestone</h2>
  <p>
    The EU ETS for shipping was phased in starting in 2024 (40% coverage) and 2025 (70%). In 2026, the mandate hit <strong>100%</strong>. This means carriers must now purchase allowances for every gram of CO₂, methane, and nitrous oxide emitted during the voyage from China to Europe.
  </p>

  <h2>The Cost Impact: By the Numbers</h2>
  <p>
    Data from Q1 2026 indicates that ETS surcharges now represent a material portion of base freight rates. For sea cargo, the average surcharge is approximately <strong>$168 per dry 40ft container</strong> from Asia to North Europe. For air freight—the primary method for Kakobuy hauls—this translates to an estimated <strong>6-8% increase</strong> in per-kg rates.
  </p>

  <div class="blog-table-wrap">
    <table>
      <thead>
