          <th>Typical Surcharge</th>
        </tr>
      </thead>
      <tbody>
        <tr>
          <td>Direct Air (CN to EU)</td>
          <td>High</td>
          <td>+$0.40 - $0.65 per kg</td>
        </tr>
        <tr>
          <td>Triangular (via UK/Non-EU)</td>
          <td>Low</td>
          <td>+$0.05 - $0.15 per kg</td>
        </tr>
        <tr>
          <td>Sea Freight (Consolidated)</td>
          <td>Moderate</td>
          <td>~7% of base rate</td>
        </tr>
      </tbody>
    </table>
  </div>

  <h2>How to Offset the Carbon Tax</h2>
  <p>
    The most effective strategy in 2026 is <strong>Routing Optimization</strong>. Since the ETS charge is calculated based on the <em>last port of call</em> before entering the EU, lines that transit through non-EU hubs (like the UK or Switzerland) often face significantly lower exposure.
  </p>
  <ul>
    <li><strong>Use "Tariffless" Lines:</strong> These lines often use complex routing that minimizes ETS-taxable legs.</li>
    <li><strong>Aggressive Consolidation:</strong> Fixed administrative fees for carbon reporting are applied per shipment. Shipping one 15kg haul is now 15-20% more cost-effective than three 5kg hauls.</li>
    <li><strong>Check the "Green Surcharge" in Dashboard:</strong> Kakobuy now breaks out these fees in the final shipping quote—look for "EMS/ESS" labels.</li>
  </ul>

  <p>
    <strong>Summary:</strong> The EU's "Fit for 55" package has made shipping a climate-cost game. Pair this knowledge with our <a href="/blog/eu-import-vat-landed-cost-spreadsheet-buyers/">EU VAT guide</a> to calculate your true landed cost in 2026.
